BSERVATION, WHICH IS REAL AND NOT ECHOED =="; echo "   Both shapes are printed by pytest itself. foundry-archive/ and .planning/"; echo "   are git-ignored, so the artefacts those two skips look for are absent in"; echo "   every detached worktree a sweep re-executes in, and each skip message"; echo "   names the worktree it looked in -- which is exactly the environmental"; echo "   variation the two grammars license, appearing on every honest"; echo "   verification and never on a forged one. The lines below are pytest's own"; echo "   skip reports, module and message, sibling line numbers stripped because a"; echo "   line number is another casting's and carries no witness."; echo; out=$(mktemp) || exit 1; uv run --quiet --with pytest pytest -rs --tb=no -q -p no:cacheprovider tests/test_measure_run.py >"$out" 2>&1; roster=$(grep '^SKIPPED' "$out" | sed -E 's/^SKIPPED \[[0-9]+\] ([^:]+):[0-9]+: /\1  /'); rm -f "$out"; planning=$(printf '%s\n' "$roster" | grep '/[.]planning/' | LC_ALL=C sort -u | head -1); archive=$(printf '%s\n' "$roster" | grep '/foundry-archive/' | LC_ALL=C sort -u | head -1); echo "== THE TWO WITNESS LINES =="; [ -n "$planning" ] && printf '   %s\n' "$planning"; [ -n "$archive" ] && printf '   %s\n' "$archive"; echo; if [ -n "$planning" ] && [ -n "$archive" ]; then echo "VERDICT: PASS -- planning_root and archive_root are both witnessed above"; exit 0; fi; echo "VERDICT: FAIL -- planning_root [$planning] archive_root [$archive]"; exit 1
